WEBVTT

00:00.280 --> 00:03.080
Six cities, two padlocked. Austin

00:03.080 --> 00:05.359
is the tutorial. Each next city

00:05.359 --> 00:06.799
unlocks when you offload a full

00:06.799 --> 00:08.599
shift in the one before.

00:08.599 --> 00:10.360
Phoenix and Las Vegas are dashed

00:10.360 --> 00:12.080
out. Robotaxis haven't launched

00:12.080 --> 00:13.960
there, so neither has the game.

00:13.960 --> 00:16.160
One bank, all six cities — not a

00:16.160 --> 00:18.320
per-city balance. A car you left

00:18.320 --> 00:19.960
parked in Miami is still billing

00:19.960 --> 00:21.400
this number at midnight while you

00:21.400 --> 00:23.680
work Tampa. Clock on and set the

00:23.680 --> 00:24.680
pace.

00:24.680 --> 00:25.960
Cars earn only while you're

00:25.960 --> 00:27.599
watching them. You're the remote

00:27.599 --> 00:31.439
operator. 1x, 4x, 20x — except in

00:31.439 --> 00:32.559
San Francisco, where you're

00:32.559 --> 00:33.840
physically in the seat and it's

00:33.840 --> 00:36.360
locked at 1x. The fleet roster.

00:36.360 --> 00:38.440
Every car, what it's doing, its

00:38.440 --> 00:40.480
charge, what it has earned today,

00:40.480 --> 00:42.520
$82, and how many rides are

00:42.520 --> 00:44.200
stacked behind the current one.

00:44.200 --> 00:46.440
Two platforms, two commissions.

00:46.440 --> 00:49.000
Hitchr takes 25% and carries 70%

00:49.000 --> 00:51.559
of demand. Zipp takes 15% and

00:51.559 --> 00:53.840
carries 30%. Your acceptance rate

00:53.840 --> 00:55.600
drives how much either sends you.

00:55.600 --> 00:58.399
The tariff, now and next. 19

00:58.399 --> 01:01.000
cents per kWh at 8 a.m., 34 from

01:01.000 --> 01:03.440
16:00. Austin Energy's real

01:03.440 --> 01:05.280
time-of-use pricing. Every city runs its

01:05.280 --> 01:07.439
own utility's published rates. Real

01:07.439 --> 01:09.560
Superchargers. Actual sites with

01:09.560 --> 01:11.720
their real stall counts, peak kW and

01:11.720 --> 01:13.840
distance. Research Boulevard never

01:13.840 --> 01:15.600
queues at 18 stalls, but charges at

01:15.600 --> 01:18.400
only 72 kW, 32 minutes away. The

01:18.400 --> 01:20.680
real geofence. Cars follow actual

01:20.680 --> 01:22.200
road geometry inside Austin's

01:22.200 --> 01:23.680
published service area. Where the

01:23.680 --> 01:25.240
real map excludes somewhere, so

01:25.240 --> 01:27.200
does this one. The selected car.

01:27.200 --> 01:29.240
Charge, range, what power costs it

01:29.240 --> 01:30.439
right now and what it would take

01:30.439 --> 01:31.960
to send it to a charger. Also,

01:31.960 --> 01:33.119
what it's worth if you sell it

01:33.119 --> 01:34.560
and what you'd still owe. The

01:34.560 --> 01:36.640
best offer and the search. One

01:36.640 --> 01:37.880
button takes the strongest job on

01:37.880 --> 01:39.520
the board. The multiplier next to

01:39.520 --> 01:41.880
it is live demand — 1.8x here

01:41.880 --> 01:43.360
because it's the morning rush. The

01:43.360 --> 01:46.040
books, broken out. Gross, net, and

01:46.040 --> 01:47.840
cost per mile. Split live into

01:47.840 --> 01:50.079
depreciation, energy, maintenance,

01:50.079 --> 01:52.000
insurance, and software.

01:52.000 --> 01:53.000
This is the panel that stops

01:53.000 --> 01:54.759
flattering you first. Three numbers

01:54.759 --> 01:57.200
per offer. $51.41 on the meter,

01:57.200 --> 01:59.600
$38.56 after commission, and 5.6

01:59.600 --> 02:00.719
miles of deadhead — empty — to reach the

02:00.719 --> 02:01.880
passenger.

02:01.880 --> 02:03.200
Only the third one decides whether

02:03.200 --> 02:04.000
you make money.
